Z||000005||PaUL||08-09-99||07:31 PM||||MR2 and CRX, thats the main reason why it was cancelled.
Z||000006||G25C||08-09-99||11:24 PM||||Its true about Chevy having the pull in GM.  And because of the Corvette made by Chevy.  It was a contributing factor to the demise of the Fiero, but a small one at that. (I read this in my High Performance Pontiac magazine).<p>This aint the first time Chevy has done this.  The Corvette is not even Chevy's idea....Its PONTIACS!!!<p>In the earlier 50 Pontiac was losing sale massively and they were trying to find a way to pick things up.  Pontiac has always been a company to make futuristic or wildly different proto type vehicles.  Well, they made the first Bonneville as a show car to atrack audiences.  This car was a 2 seat sports car with a straight 8 and 8 single barrel carbs.  It looked very close to what the Corvette came to be when it came out.<p>The Bonneville had a bubble canopy top and what looked like a turbine engine outlet on the back. (wasnt real, just for looks).  Like i said, this was a proto type to improve sales and get the attention of the younger crowd. <p>Well, Chevy went to the Brass and said hey Pontiac cant offord to produce that car (at this time Pontiac sales were so bad that it was even considered to drop Pontiac completely from GM.)<p>Chevy also said that there was know way in hell that a car like that would sell.  So the brass and the bean counters took into account that it was just impratical....For PONTIAC!  But NOT for Cheverolet, who promptly produced a Corvette that amazingly enough look like the Bonneville (there are 2 of these left) that they said wouldnt sell!!!<p>Then Semon "bunkie" Knudsen turned Pontiac and there slow sales around and realy put a hurten on Chevy sales.<p>BUT WAIT THATS NOT ALL.<p>In 64 John DeLorean secretly made a sports car with off the shelf parts and presented it to GM.  Do you know what it was called?  If you said the GTO your wrong! (although he did that too).<p>This was called the BANSHEE SP6.  and it would have been a Corvette killer indeed!  It featured off the shelf Tempest parts (trying to make it cheap to win the bean counters hearts).  It looked much like the Corvette but the front end had a small crome nose that looked like the 67 Firebirds...but much thinner and smaller.<p>It had a 326 base engine (280 hp) and and a price at 2,500!  Just think of what would have happened to this car when Royal Bobcat would have gotten a hold of it!<p>Well, Chevy screamed and GM dropped the idea and forgot it ever happened.  I think a fella out west owns 2 of them.<p>If you looked at it.  Pontiac is the performance leader for GM that the other GM divisions look to for ideas.<p>The GTO was first<br>The Grand Prix was GM's first luxery permormance car.<br>The Camaro might have came out first, but Pontiac was making Firebird concepts in the earier 60's.<br>Hell, even the transport was Pontiacs idea back in 88, but Chevy had to have one too.<p>Chevy makes me sick!<p>Thats all ive have to say about that, 
Z||000007||ChadMan||08-10-99||06:49 AM||||I think the Fiero was cancelled because they made too many of them.  I read that Mazda has never sold more than 25,000 Miatas in one model year, and it's heralded as a huge success.  The Fiero sold more than 150,000 units in its first two years.  I think Pontiac (+ MR2, RX7, CRX) saturated the sports-car market.  Increasing insurance costs also contributed.<p>If Pontiac had limited production to 30,000 units per year and charged more for them, the Fiero would probably still be around.  Of course, I wouldn't be able to afford one!
Z||000008||DJRice||08-10-99||07:21 AM||||The thing I like most about my Fiero is that it has <b>character</b>.  It has a look that maintains its style.  If you were to put any model Pontiac side to side with its sister car in any other division, you will see that the Pontiac just has more character.<p>Except the new 30th Anniversary Firebird Ram Air, that car does not have character, it <b>is</b> character.  If Darth Vader needed a car, it would be that one!<p>BTW, I read an article about the demise of the Fiero, Ill have to find the link and post it.
